cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RoadForge in research or an engineering project, please cite this software."
title: "RoadForge: A Simulation-to-Model Workbench for Road-Scene Semantic Perception"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jafari
    given-names: Arvin
    affiliation: Independent Developer
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
url: "https://github.com/ArvinNotDev/RoadForge"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArvinNotDev/RoadForge"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  RoadForge is a Windows-first desktop workbench for collecting road-scene RGB
  data from CARLA, generating YOLOPv2 ONNX teacher pseudo-labels, auditing and
  preparing semantic-segmentation datasets, fine-tuning YOLO26 semantic models,
  evaluating checkpoints, and validating ONNX deployment artifacts.
keywords:
  - autonomous driving
  - CARLA
  - semantic segmentation
  - pseudo-labeling
  - dataset curation
  - YOLO26
  - ONNX
